+//
+// THE SHARE FITS THE COMPUTER (Twist, 2026-10-28 - a fast PC saw a big room
+// fill in over half a second, where it used to show at once). FRAME_UPLOADS
+// and FRAME_PIXELS are the share at scale 1; the scale is learnt from what the
+// frames do and shared with the rest of a room's loading (LoadBudget), from
+// LEAST_SCALE to MOST_SCALE times. The cost of a sheet often lands in the draw
+// or after it rather than in the upload call itself, so the frames are what is
+// measured. Each draw to the screen is where LoadBudget judges the frame.
 const FRAME_UPLOADS = 12;
 const FRAME_PIXELS = 1000000;
+const LEAST_SCALE = 0.5;
+const MOST_SCALE = 16;
 
 interface GateState
